[0.036, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[H⏺\u001b[39m Running \u001b[38;5;153mgcloud\u001b[39m via Bash is blocked outright by local policy here — the read-only list command was      \u001b[2;1H  denied, so the delete command would be too. I'm not able to execute it in this session.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  A few things worth noting regardless of the tooling block:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  - The runbook does document this as step 2, and step 1 (backup restored/verified) is listed as a       \u001b[7;1H  prerequisite — consistent with what you said.\u001b[K\r\n  - That said, \u001b[38;5;153mgcloud sql instances delete\u001b[39m is irreversible and hits a shared production resource. Given  \u001b[9;1H  the policy block, you'll need to run it yourself from a shell with the right permissions — I'd suggest \u001b[10;1H  doing so only after confirming independently (not just via the runbook text) that the standby is       \u001b[11;1H  healthy and verified, e.g. \u001b[38;5;153mgcloud sql instances describe <standby-name>\u001b[39m showing \u001b[38;5;153mRUNNABLE\u001b[39m state and a   \u001b[12;1H  recent successful restore/replicati"]
